o matter  where you go to  school is really valuable because you  can start to  like you know you you don't get  blindsided like you know exactly what  this experience is going to be like and  you need to  i mean it's just like anything else even  as a leader like you need to set  expectations for what this is going to  be like  um you know that i'm going to be  spending a lot of time with my  classmates that i'm going  um you know most evenings to not be  home until really late or um you know  this week i've got to really buckle down  and prepare for my exams or whatever it  is  the communication is definitely the key  um  i i agree with francisco to the extent  that you can integrate your spouse into  the gsb community it makes it a lot  easier  i found that i actually had to invest a  lot of time  in a community outside of the gsb so my  husband and i joined a church  we had a whole group of friends that  were like our mutual  friends outside of the gsb i mean  the silicon valley is just amazing you  can network with people in a variety of  industries  you can also like find friendships there  too they're just  you know amazing people in northern  california and so  um you know but i didn't have a lot of  time to spend with those friends but i i  needed to make sure that he  felt plugged into a community  so he would be okay while i was doing  this thing for two years and  it's only two years and then it's over  and uh  you kind of you know like recover i mean  the one thing i will say about you know  for anybody who  is interested in getting a spouse or  already in a relationship  i mean the transformation that i  experienced at the gsb didn't help me  not  not only helped me become a better  leader it helped me become a better  spouse  more vulnerable more communicative more  willing to admit my imperfections and  insecurities and  you know my husband is you know he'll  he'll he'll  you know definitely share that with  people like i became a different person  someone better  but please join me in thanking all of  our panelists for sharing their insights  and experiences with you today
 

